    "summary": "Saint Stephen finale, jam‑heavy electric set with tight acoustic moments",
    "blurb": "The June 5 1970 Fillmore West show features a soaring Saint Stephen > Casey Jones encore and strong mid‑set jams on Black Peter, New Speedway Boogie and The Other One. Acoustic highlights include crystal‑clear I Know You Rider and vocal harmonies that keep the energy high.",
    "review": "On June 5, 1970 at the Fillmore West the Dead delivered a memorable two‑set plus encore that captures the band in fine mid‑70s form. The first set rolls through folk‑rock staples – Dire Wolf, I Know You Rider and Black Peter – with Garcia’s voice ringing clear on the acoustic numbers and his guitar cutting through the electric tracks. Set two builds momentum with Easy Wind and a blistering run through The Other One, punctuated by a wild “GODDAMMIT!” from Bob. The night closes with a fiery Saint Stephen that segues into a rousing Casey Jones, leaving the audience buzzing. Across the available recordings the soundboard captures are solid but patchy, while the miced‑stage matrix (gd1970-06-05.132395.bear.wise.flac16) offers the clearest overall mix despite a slightly boomier drum presence.",
